{"title":"2026 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 2026 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are 2026 integers greater than 1 written on a blackboard, not necessarily different. In a move, Confucius chooses two integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cce1bd621aff652b0983cbc94a24545e5f4bdcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> from different places on the blackboard and replaces the two integers with\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70a2f03b6ab6c46e033d068c8ab550af5d1bfec5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\gcd(m,n) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{\\operatorname{lcm}(m,n)}{\\gcd(m,n)}.\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>He continues to make moves while it is possible to do so. \n</p><p>(a). Prove that, regardless of the choices of Confucius, after finitely many moves, exactly one integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> on the blackboard is greater than 1.\n</p><p>(b). Prove that the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> does not depend on the choices of Confucius. \n</p><p>(Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75c1d5e24ac094e4b383e8c7034d2bddb95c570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the greatest common divisor of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/1940a0fbb129cd6ebaebfc3d5ba42d8082219659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{lcm}(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the least common multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle and let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoints of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be chosen strictly inside triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1a0f691e308462e4fe9b0476508ef0b065423c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMC$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d89d48d3a98b680786ac9610fb170be757efa8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BNC$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> lies strictly inside triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/25697024d81a441f727e279d2216eeb169abced9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABL$\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> lies strictly inside triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f7934b5d8a33ac82751385e6b510779e126ccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff74314fa0a661df96136e3d8549fd8bebf164b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle KBA = \\angle ACL, \\quad \\angle LBK = \\angle LNC, \\quad \\angle LCK = \\angle BMK.\\]\" width=\"467\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcentre of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7439149f594e9b8f42ef995654a5cf9d644b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKL$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb10d6a438df5c7f083e8f5b8c53c9d48538983.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OM = ON.\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer.\n</p><p>Liu Bang and Xiang Yu have a stick of side length 1 and want to divide it between themselves. Liu marks at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points on the stick, and then Xiang marks at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points on the stick. The marked points are distinct. Then, the stick is cut at all marked points, creating a number of pieces. Afterwards, they take turns claiming any unclaimed piece of the stick, with Liu going first. Each player's goal is to maximize the total length of their own pieces.\n</p><p>For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, determine the largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that Liu may guarantee a total length of at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, regardless of Xiang's play.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Shan-Yu and Mulan are playing a game. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be an angle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12c8cdfce7133f5fef523411a812812cf2ae3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ &lt; \\theta &lt; 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" /> known to both players. Initially, Shan-Yu makes a paper triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with measurements of his choice. They repeatedly form the following steps.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has at least one angle measuring exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the game stops and Mulan wins.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Otherwise, Mulan chooses a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, different from its three vertices. She then makes a straight cut from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the opposite vertex of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Shan-Yu discards one of the two triangles. The remaining triangle becomes the new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812a5bf65a623b4fb2fddedb8c99a2b981265d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{T}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>For which real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can Mulan guarantee her victory in finitely many steps, no matter how Shan-Yu plays?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/72457cb47799159bbe79b8bbda486a478835b6a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of all positive real numbers. Determine all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60cfda1606f9e29d1b4a14ab8af5985d96ba6d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a99592f23e8d47e4abd6208ea55c7d065c380bd4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{x^2 + f(y)^2}{2}} \\geq \\frac{f(x)+y}{2} \\geq \\sqrt{xf(y)}\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"43\" />\nfor every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe59bfb5581aba06e19d564232fa937bee10774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d745b81add053aa31f45d72cb9a898e3441e74bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, a_3, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> be an infinite sequence of positive integers greater than 1.\n</p><p>Suppose that for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cfb07e4911e7b4f994b858f3d47604ddbee438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the smallest positive integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b08555e71e4aa0335936fecd3cdfb45a0040f1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a_{n+1}, a_i) &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8fda85b509471f117cb6e73b2680da394de5fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1, 2, \\dots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Prove that there exist positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03cc91d3d9debb09b31c0f2ddee3a807762c5bf8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n+T}  = a_n + L\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" />\nfor every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>(Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75c1d5e24ac094e4b383e8c7034d2bddb95c570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the greatest common divisor of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO\" title=\"2026 IMO\">2026 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions resources\">Mathematics competitions resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO\" title=\"2026 IMO\">2026 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO\" title=\"2025 IMO\">2025 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 IMO Problem